      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَشّج القَرَابَةَ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَوْشِيجٌ</span>, (tropical:)  <i>He</i> (God)
<i>made the relationship intricate.</i> (S, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وشّج</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اللّٰهُ بَيْنَهُمْ</span> (tropical:)  <i>God joined and mixed them together.</i>
(TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وشّج</span> <i>He laced together</i> a <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَحْمِل</span> [or
basket in which grapes are carried to the dryingplace] <i>with a leather thong,</i> or <i>the like,</i> (such as
a <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَرِيط</span>, TA,) lest anything should fall from
it. (K.)

